      "url": "https://www.last.fm/music/Creedence+Clearwater+Revival/Bayou+Country",
      "wiki_content": "Bayou Country is the second album by American band Creedence Clearwater Revival, released in 1969. It was CCR's first album to be certified Platinum, and would go on to multi-platinum status. The album's single \"Proud Mary/Born on the Bayou\" was also the band's first gold single. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Creedence+Clearwater+Revival/Bayou+Country\">Read more on Last.fm</a>. User-contributed text is available under the Creative Commons By-SA License; additional terms may apply.",
      "wiki_summary": "Bayou Country is the second album by American band Creedence Clearwater Revival, released in 1969. It was CCR's first album to be certified Platinum, and would go on to multi-platinum status. The album's single \"Proud Mary/Born on the Bayou\" was also the band's first gold single. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Creedence+Clearwater+Revival/Bayou+Country\">Read more on Last.fm</a>."
    },
    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Bayou Country is Creedence Clearwater Revival’s second studio album, released in 1969 on Fantasy, and it’s the record where the band fully locked into its signature swamp-rock identity. Led by John Fogerty’s distinctive vocals and sharp songwriting, the album blends hard-driving rock with blues, country, and Southern-flavored atmosphere, even though the band itself was from California. Its best-known track, “Proud Mary,” became a major hit and helped establish CCR as one of the defining American rock bands of the era.\n\nThe album is especially noted for its dark, murky opening with “Born on the Bayou,” its gritty momentum, and its stripped-down, muscular sound. While some early critics felt the material was uneven, later listeners and reviewers have often praised its intensity, consistency of mood, and the way it sharpened the band’s style after their debut. Bayou Country remains an important early statement of Creedence Clearwater Revival’s earthy, rootsy approach to rock.",
